- 28: AAAA record.
Specify an integer. Do not use the string A or AAAA.', example='1'),
          typeLabel?: string(name='TypeLabel', description='The auxiliary display text for the record type. This text is not used for matching or DNS resolution decisions. You can omit this parameter in the request.', example='A'),
          weight?: int32(name='Weight', description='The relative weight of the record. This parameter is used to select one record of the same queried type only when ResultMode is set to 1. We recommend that you set this parameter to a positive integer from 1 to 100. The sum of the weights of all records does not need to be 100. This parameter is not used for selection when ResultMode is set to 0.', example='100'),
        }
      ](name='Records', description='The list of configured DNS records. The list can include A and AAAA records. Actual DNS resolution returns only the records of the queried type. If the list is empty or does not contain records of the queried type, the system continues to fall back.'),
      resultMode?: int32(name='ResultMode', description='The record return mode. Valid values:
- 0: Returns all records of the queried type.
- 1: Returns one record of the queried type based on the weight.', example='0'),
      ttl?: int32(name='Ttl', description='The cache validity period of the record, in seconds. The value must be a positive integer.', example='60'),
    }
  ](name='Rules', description='The complete list of rules. This parameter is required and must contain at least one rule. If you match only by IP address range, you can configure a default rule without ArgKeys and Args, and configure the A or AAAA destination addresses in the Records field of the rule. The update replaces the original rule list as a whole. Old rules that are not included in the new list are removed. When the rules are saved, the serialized UTF-8 JSON content must be less than 65,535 bytes.', shrink='json', position='Body'),
}

